  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, in a profile you're not able to add a discord URL, there is a little known feature in Discord where if you have a URL where it follows the format: \"discord://-/users/{YOUR USER ID}\" it opens the discord client. It would be great to be able to just add this to my profile instead of adding a server of mine.\n\nThe first attached image is the example of the URL for me with my ID blurred out, the second one is my profile with details blurred out. There are a few ways to do this, two of which being:\n\n- allow the discord:// protocol to be entered, this could be insecure as you could take the user to settings.\n\n- allow a user to enter a Discord ID, a check would make sure it's entirely numeric and prepend the discord user part of the URL.\n\nI feel this feature would fix the problems of connecting Discord to a profile whilst also not being **too** hard to implement.",
